      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot even begin to fully grasp the depth of what you're going through – it sounds like you're experiencing a profound sense of loss that we can't truly comprehend. The idea of rebirth and rediscovery might seem overwhelming when you believe your core has been damaged or 'obliterated.' It's okay to feel this way. Healing and rebuilding from whatever loss you've felt is a journey that takes time, despite how it might seem. Have you considered finding support to help with these emotions, such as a grief counselor or a support group? There may be ways to cope and find meaning again at a pace that's right for you.",
      "source": "target",
